WEBVTT

01:44.354 --> 01:46.397
I'm gonna drink on his tab.

01:51.319 --> 01:52.153
Okay.

01:55.156 --> 01:57.826
We're already in the middle of the city.

01:57.909 --> 01:59.702
We might as well have fun.

02:00.703 --> 02:02.163
Time to learn about the world.

02:03.998 --> 02:06.417
It's time to learn about the world!

02:38.158 --> 02:40.910
The outside world's horses
are big and fast.

02:40.994 --> 02:43.079
Riding them would take
some getting used to.

02:43.163 --> 02:45.915
I liked that horse that finished first.

02:45.999 --> 02:47.834
I wonder how much it would cost.

02:47.917 --> 02:50.712
Don't. Hana-chan would divorce me.

02:50.795 --> 02:53.089
I'll buy you whatever you
need to live down here.

02:53.840 --> 02:54.924
Horses and cattle.

02:55.008 --> 02:56.426
As long as it's not livestock.

02:57.176 --> 03:00.471
Besides that, what I need most is arrows.

03:00.555 --> 03:03.808
I've got a bow at your house,
but I lack arrows.

03:03.892 --> 03:07.312
Arrows, huh? Where do they sell those?

03:07.395 --> 03:10.064
I can make my own if I have the materials.

03:18.197 --> 03:20.366
All of this is for sale?

03:20.450 --> 03:21.534
Yup.

03:21.618 --> 03:22.452
TOOLS

03:22.535 --> 03:24.370
What do you need to make arrows?

03:24.454 --> 03:26.998
Arrow bamboo, thread, and a knife.

03:27.749 --> 03:29.709
I can use iron or stone
for the arrowheads.

03:29.792 --> 03:31.044
What about the fletching?

03:31.127 --> 03:34.005
We've got the feathers from the pheasant
I sold you the other day.

03:34.797 --> 03:37.425
- Do they sell whole deer?
- A deer?

03:38.009 --> 03:40.470
I'll boil the skin and organs
to make animal glue.

03:40.553 --> 03:42.138
Please don't.

03:42.222 --> 03:44.474
We'd get complaints at the apartment.

03:45.058 --> 03:46.059
Use this.

03:47.268 --> 03:49.312
It's wood glue.

03:49.395 --> 03:50.438
What is that?

03:50.521 --> 03:52.440
Check it out.

03:52.523 --> 03:54.192
That's so convenient!

03:54.275 --> 03:55.109
REGISTER

03:55.193 --> 03:56.319
Welcome.

03:57.612 --> 04:00.031
They've got everything down here.

04:06.829 --> 04:10.458
One item, two items, three items.

04:11.793 --> 04:14.337
Thank you.

04:15.797 --> 04:17.048
Boss,

04:17.131 --> 04:20.176
I'm hallucinating. Could I take a break?

04:20.260 --> 04:23.388
What? Quit screwing around
and do your job.

04:23.471 --> 04:25.181
I'm being exploited!

04:25.974 --> 04:29.936
That girl could see us.

04:30.019 --> 04:32.647
She doesn't seem like a Daemon wielder.

04:32.730 --> 04:36.442
She just happened to be able
to see you, like Left said.

04:36.526 --> 04:39.404
Sometimes people see them
when they're sleep deprived.

04:39.487 --> 04:41.239
CLOTHING

04:41.823 --> 04:43.157
We should pick up clothes, too.

04:46.703 --> 04:47.745
A scarecrow?!

04:51.958 --> 04:55.295
I like that the clothes down here
have lots of storage compartments.

04:55.378 --> 04:57.338
Pick whatever you'd like.

04:58.131 --> 05:01.843
I prefer black. It hides bloodstains.

05:01.926 --> 05:04.887
What an edgelord, choosing his clothes
to hide bloodstains.

05:05.722 --> 05:07.390
- What about underwear?
- What are these?

05:07.473 --> 05:08.850
They're called underpants.

05:08.933 --> 05:10.143
They're the evolved form of loincloths.

05:10.727 --> 05:13.146
I don't like these. I prefer loincloths.

05:14.147 --> 05:16.607
Excuse me. Do you carry loincloths?

05:16.691 --> 05:18.526
No, sorry.

05:19.193 --> 05:20.486
Oh, right.

05:21.612 --> 05:26.868
I was attacked by bandits a few times
while hunting on my own.

05:28.077 --> 05:33.458
I killed anyone trying to kill me
like my father taught me.

05:33.541 --> 05:36.044
I buried the bodies
or let streams carry them away,

05:36.127 --> 05:38.129
but something always felt off.

05:38.713 --> 05:41.632
I've finally solved that mystery.

05:42.300 --> 05:45.636
All the bandits who attacked me
were too clean.

05:46.471 --> 05:50.349
Adults of a certain age
who live in the mountains

05:50.433 --> 05:55.938
have dirt on their nails and knuckles
that just won't wash off.

05:56.731 --> 05:58.066
But all the bandits

05:58.149 --> 06:01.486
had clean hands like you,
and you live down here.

06:01.986 --> 06:05.865
And one of them was wearing
these underpants things.

06:06.365 --> 06:08.159
What are you, a highwayman?

06:08.743 --> 06:13.498
They came up the mountain to kill me.

06:13.581 --> 06:14.999
They'd lose your trust

06:15.083 --> 06:18.419
if you came back
after a villager killed you.

06:18.503 --> 06:22.673
You'd think you gained Seal
after an outsider killed you,

06:22.757 --> 06:24.967
and the village could
keep their hold on you.

06:25.676 --> 06:28.596
We don't know yet that
the village sent the bandits.

06:29.097 --> 06:32.016
But I can't trust them completely...

06:32.600 --> 06:35.478
What if something happens
while you're alone in the mountains?

06:35.561 --> 06:37.688
even though I want to.

06:38.606 --> 06:44.529
Only a few others and I know how
to enter Higashi Village's barrier.

06:45.113 --> 06:47.615
Good. That narrows it down a lot.

06:48.699 --> 06:50.618
Will we attack them?

06:50.701 --> 06:53.329
Yeah. We'll seize the initiative.

06:53.412 --> 06:55.540
I thought you might say that.

06:56.582 --> 06:59.627
When hunting, whoever claims
the best position first wins.

07:00.711 --> 07:02.547
- Anyway, Dera-san.
- Yeah?

07:03.673 --> 07:04.799
We're being followed.

07:04.882 --> 07:07.051
Yeah. By three, I think.

07:07.635 --> 07:10.263
One, two, three.

07:10.346 --> 07:12.056
They're taking turns tailing us.

07:12.140 --> 07:14.267
Are they Kagemoris?

07:14.350 --> 07:16.769
Man, those guys are a piece of work.

07:16.853 --> 07:18.062
Don't look behind you.

07:18.146 --> 07:19.397
Got it.

07:20.148 --> 07:22.900
Dera-san, you said
you didn't want to be found,

07:22.984 --> 07:27.572
but you were in that... picture Asa made.

07:28.156 --> 07:30.783
That could be used to identify you.

07:30.867 --> 07:32.076
Oh, that's fine.

07:32.160 --> 07:36.080
Mansions like those shell out
for security cameras everywhere.

07:36.873 --> 07:39.333
Shell out?

07:39.417 --> 07:42.086
I accounted for my face
being seen at some point

07:42.170 --> 07:45.298
when I decided to go there.

07:50.636 --> 07:52.305
Brother...

07:58.436 --> 08:01.689
Where's my photo editing app?

08:02.773 --> 08:03.816
There.

08:03.900 --> 08:08.404
Asa-san, you took a picture
of Tadera earlier, didn't you?

08:08.488 --> 08:10.323
Dera-san's not in the picture.

08:10.406 --> 08:12.325
He's potentially dangerous.

08:12.408 --> 08:14.035
If we have information on him...

08:14.118 --> 08:15.495
What? He's not in it?

08:15.578 --> 08:16.704
Nope.

08:17.205 --> 08:19.040
Wasn't he in the picture
with your brother?

08:19.123 --> 08:20.333
Nope.

08:21.334 --> 08:25.963
Haruo, check the gate's security
camera footage for Tadera.

08:27.882 --> 08:30.885
If my brother's in it,
send those bits to me.

08:33.095 --> 08:36.974
The bearded guy
in the camo jacket is Akishima.

08:37.475 --> 08:40.144
He said he'd find us illicit work.

08:40.645 --> 08:43.523
He contacted us about a well-paying job.

08:44.148 --> 08:46.025
This is my call history.

08:46.108 --> 08:49.987
You can see that
he called me yesterday at midnight.

08:50.071 --> 08:52.532
I got a call around the same time.

08:53.950 --> 08:58.079
I think he called everyone nearby
who could come right away.

08:58.162 --> 09:02.375
Like we said, we met everyone
on the team for the first time.

09:02.875 --> 09:06.295
Midnight's around the time
we finished our fight with Yuru

09:06.379 --> 09:08.130
and were driving here.

09:08.798 --> 09:12.134
That's when Jin-san called me.

09:12.718 --> 09:15.179
What time did you enter the manor?

09:15.263 --> 09:18.474
I think it was between 1:30
and just before 2:00.

09:18.558 --> 09:21.394
That's when you came
to get your leg treated.

09:21.477 --> 09:22.395
Right.

09:22.478 --> 09:25.523
This manor is surrounded by a barrier.

09:25.606 --> 09:31.404
Only clan members and their guests
can enter the gate at that time.

09:32.071 --> 09:38.202
Was there a Kagemori by the gate
at that time who invited you inside?

09:38.286 --> 09:41.872
Beardy-Akishima was the only person there.

09:41.956 --> 09:44.292
Actually, the west gate was open.

09:44.375 --> 09:45.793
We got in easily.

09:45.876 --> 09:46.794
Right?

09:47.378 --> 09:51.132
We were told the manor
was full of Daemons,

09:51.215 --> 09:53.134
so we'd blend in once we were inside.

09:53.217 --> 09:56.846
Wait, wait, wait. Which gate?

09:56.929 --> 09:58.472
What? The west gate.

09:59.515 --> 10:02.810
There's no west gate at this manor.

10:02.893 --> 10:04.020
What?

10:04.103 --> 10:05.563
What? But there is.

10:05.646 --> 10:07.315
There isn't.

10:08.065 --> 10:12.069
There is no west gate
at the Kagemori manor.

10:12.153 --> 10:14.322
The entire west side is a wall.

10:15.740 --> 10:17.074
Fuyuki.

10:17.158 --> 10:17.992
Yes, sir.

10:23.080 --> 10:25.416
What are you doing to my partners?

10:25.499 --> 10:28.252
Don't worry. He won't kill them.

10:28.919 --> 10:31.255
This Daemon pair is Kori-Henge.

10:31.339 --> 10:35.217
Their current individual names
are Akai-san and Midori-san.

10:35.801 --> 10:38.179
Their current master is Tachikawa Makoto.

10:38.262 --> 10:41.432
She was born on May 4th, 1997.

10:41.515 --> 10:44.268
She completed some undergraduate
studies at Ariake Women's University.

10:44.352 --> 10:45.269
She currently resides

10:45.353 --> 10:47.229
- in Shinkiba, Koto-ku, Tokyo.
- Wha...

10:47.813 --> 10:50.316
She has one younger sister
and one younger brother.

10:50.399 --> 10:53.527
Her parents divorced on August, 2008,

10:53.611 --> 10:55.571
and her mother received
full custody of her.

10:55.655 --> 10:57.657
Her mother is currently being
treated in a hospital.

10:57.740 --> 10:59.533
She is currently unemployed.

10:59.617 --> 11:00.993
- She accepted this job
- Wait, wait, wait.

11:01.077 --> 11:03.079
- to cover her mother's hospital bills.
- Oh, excuse me.

11:03.162 --> 11:07.166
It's not right to expose
a woman's personal information.

11:07.750 --> 11:09.168
Or a man's.

11:09.251 --> 11:12.463
Whisper, could you stop speaking
for a moment?

11:12.546 --> 11:13.672
Sure thing.

11:17.259 --> 11:18.969
Okay, good.

11:19.053 --> 11:20.346
What the hell was that?

11:21.138 --> 11:22.848
Embrace, next.

11:25.309 --> 11:26.685
Be gentle.

11:26.769 --> 11:28.604
I'm always gentle.

11:29.313 --> 11:30.648
Pair name: Yin-Yang.

11:30.731 --> 11:32.274
Currently no individual names.

11:32.358 --> 11:34.193
Their current master is Asa-san.

11:34.693 --> 11:37.029
Their previous master is Hamura Kenichi.

11:37.113 --> 11:41.200
He was born on June 16th, 1992.

11:41.700 --> 11:43.119
He currently resides in...

11:44.245 --> 11:45.621
I see.

11:46.997 --> 11:48.624
Gambling debt, huh?

11:49.291 --> 11:51.168
They're both telling the truth.

11:51.252 --> 11:53.254
They really met on the job.

11:53.337 --> 11:56.632
Who's this guy stomping all over the Act
on the Protection of Personal Information?

11:56.715 --> 11:58.300
Kuroya Fuyuki.

11:58.801 --> 12:01.929
This Daemon pair is Blacklist.

12:02.012 --> 12:03.264
By touching Daemons,

12:03.347 --> 12:07.351
they extract information
on their previous masters.

12:07.852 --> 12:13.441
Now we know you're just mercs
with no connections to the mastermind.

12:14.692 --> 12:17.486
If you're broke, why not work for us?

12:17.570 --> 12:18.737
What?

12:18.821 --> 12:22.533
I mean, we'd appreciate jobs, but...

12:22.616 --> 12:24.493
You're not going to punish us?

12:26.120 --> 12:28.038
You'll work like horses.

12:30.249 --> 12:32.585
Are your mother's
hospital bills expensive?

12:33.169 --> 12:35.588
Y-Yes. Her condition's hard to treat.

12:35.671 --> 12:37.840
We'll cover all her expenses.

12:37.923 --> 12:41.218
Have her focus on getting better.

12:41.969 --> 12:43.387
Thank you!

12:43.471 --> 12:44.847
Could you pay off my debt—

12:46.474 --> 12:49.185
You'll have to work hard for your pay.

12:49.768 --> 12:53.063
You can start by helping us
tidy up the manor.

12:53.147 --> 12:55.524
Y-Yes, sir!

12:57.193 --> 12:59.153
Are you sure we should let them live?

12:59.236 --> 13:00.488
It's fine.

13:00.571 --> 13:04.366
We know who they are
and have their personal details.

13:04.950 --> 13:08.120
Keep them on as expendable soldiers.

13:08.204 --> 13:09.914
Yes, sir.

13:10.414 --> 13:13.542
What should we do with
the other Daemon wielders we captured?

13:13.626 --> 13:15.794
Have masters whose
Daemons died in the attack

13:15.878 --> 13:18.672
form contracts with new Daemons later.

13:18.756 --> 13:21.133
And use Blacklist
to get their information.

13:25.471 --> 13:27.640
If you figure out who the mastermind is,

13:27.723 --> 13:31.477
kill them and everyone
associated with them.

13:31.977 --> 13:33.771
Yes, sir.

13:44.406 --> 13:48.118
Hey, miss. Could I get my Daemons back?

13:49.203 --> 13:51.622
Did you come up with names for them?

13:51.705 --> 13:54.208
Oh, uh...

13:54.959 --> 13:56.877
Ohagi and Daifuku?

13:57.962 --> 13:58.796
What?

14:01.173 --> 14:03.634
How cute.

14:03.717 --> 14:06.595
What? I've got a sweet tooth, okay?

14:06.679 --> 14:10.015
I wasn't expecting such peaceful names
from someone who looks and acts like you.

14:10.099 --> 14:11.809
Shut up!

14:11.892 --> 14:15.771
Says the guy who named his Daemons
Ai-chan and Makoto-kun.

14:15.854 --> 14:17.856
What are your teeth called?

14:18.649 --> 14:25.322
Joe William Frederic Gabriel I
and Kirk Douglas Auldglaive Gabriel II.

14:25.948 --> 14:28.450
Those names are such a mouthful
they're giving me heartburn.

14:29.493 --> 14:32.204
Sorry, sorry, sorry!

14:32.288 --> 14:37.126
Well? He seems sorry,
and he gave you cute names.

14:37.209 --> 14:38.460
Want to go back to him?

14:41.547 --> 14:42.715
They don't want to.

14:42.798 --> 14:44.133
What?

14:44.216 --> 14:47.553
People don't change that quickly.

14:47.636 --> 14:50.055
I'll hold onto them a little longer.

14:50.639 --> 14:51.974
Get to work.

14:53.809 --> 14:56.770
Break doesn't have any objections
to you keeping them?

14:56.854 --> 15:00.107
Nope. No response so far.

15:00.190 --> 15:02.318
I guess we're compatible with Yin-Yang.

15:02.401 --> 15:05.529
Why not keep them forever?

15:05.613 --> 15:08.115
The more eyes keeping
you safe, the better.

15:09.366 --> 15:10.784
You're right.

15:11.869 --> 15:15.915
There could still be enemies
inside the manor.

15:17.875 --> 15:20.711
MEETING IN PROGRESS
DO NOT ENTER

15:21.295 --> 15:22.963
That was close.

15:23.047 --> 15:26.717
I panicked when we went off schedule.

15:26.800 --> 15:29.762
Sorry for the trouble, Nakagami-san.

15:29.845 --> 15:31.472
I'll do better next time.

15:31.555 --> 15:32.932
What should we do for next time?

15:33.015 --> 15:35.059
Hire more people?

15:35.142 --> 15:39.480
I could introduce you to
some part-timers who can start right away.

15:39.563 --> 15:42.232
No, I don't need anyone else.

15:42.900 --> 15:46.612
I've learned that Gabby-chan
and Asa-chan are actually pretty useful.

15:47.363 --> 15:49.323
You don't need any help?

15:49.406 --> 15:52.618
No, I'll figure it out.

15:53.202 --> 15:58.374
Anyway, I really thought
I'd miss my deadline this time.

15:58.958 --> 16:01.794
That's the closest I've ever cut it.

16:01.877 --> 16:05.756
All my assistants got sick,
and I lost my files.

16:05.839 --> 16:08.884
We were so behind schedule, I panicked.

16:08.968 --> 16:11.303
Yeah, that was almost a disaster.

16:11.387 --> 16:14.264
Negotiating with the printers wasn't easy.

16:14.348 --> 16:16.308
I'm really sorry for the trouble.

16:16.892 --> 16:19.061
I'll manage my schedule better next time.

16:19.645 --> 16:21.939
And I don't need more assistants.

16:22.022 --> 16:26.151
Gabby-chan and Asa-chan have been
helping me finish my pages recently.

16:26.235 --> 16:30.114
Oh, those girls you mention all the time?

16:30.197 --> 16:31.782
They're good girls.

16:31.865 --> 16:33.701
I hope you're paying them.

16:34.326 --> 16:35.703
Of course I am.

16:36.286 --> 16:40.416
Anyway, why is your room
so dark, Hagure-sensei?

16:40.499 --> 16:43.711
You look like the boss
of an evil organization.

16:43.794 --> 16:48.215
Our house got wrecked,
and part of it doesn't have power.

16:51.010 --> 16:52.011
Good.

16:52.094 --> 16:54.680
These are easier to move in
than those sandal things.

16:57.808 --> 16:59.435
They're still following us.

16:59.518 --> 17:02.104
A simple change of clothes
isn't a disguise.

17:02.187 --> 17:05.691
I was thinking we could
turn the tables on them,

17:05.774 --> 17:07.985
but I took your machete without asking

17:08.068 --> 17:11.405
and forgot it
at the Kagemori manor. Sorry.

17:11.488 --> 17:15.701
We'd have a problem if you started
swinging a machete around in the city,

17:15.784 --> 17:16.869
so it's all good.

17:17.828 --> 17:21.206
If you want a weapon,
should we stop by my place?

17:21.290 --> 17:23.083
I'd like to arm myself, too.

17:23.167 --> 17:25.377
Is your home nearby?

17:25.461 --> 17:26.462
It's a short walk.

17:27.671 --> 17:30.382
We don't have to defeat our tails?

17:30.466 --> 17:32.551
They'll find out where you live.

17:32.634 --> 17:34.386
Let them follow us.

17:34.970 --> 17:39.600
I was planning to abandon the place,
but I'll use it a while longer.

17:47.191 --> 17:48.901
It's like a maze.

17:48.984 --> 17:52.654
Stay close. You'll get lost.

18:12.716 --> 18:16.136
In here. You can keep your shoes on.

18:24.686 --> 18:27.022
Take whatever you want.

18:31.735 --> 18:33.862
I sense Daemons.

18:33.946 --> 18:36.031
- What?
- Yeah, I bet.

18:40.202 --> 18:42.538
That's Tadera's crib?

18:42.621 --> 18:44.331
Let's not chase them too far.

18:44.414 --> 18:45.415
We're heading back.

18:45.499 --> 18:47.668
We'll report this location
to the higher ups.

18:47.751 --> 18:49.044
Aw, c'mon.

18:51.130 --> 18:52.297
At least stay for tea.

18:59.930 --> 19:01.306
Damn it.

19:12.818 --> 19:16.071
Welcome to the Tadera clan's Lost House.

19:16.738 --> 19:20.033
There's just a thin layer separating
this world from the one we came from,

19:20.117 --> 19:23.829
but I'm the only one
who knows the route in and out.

19:23.912 --> 19:28.250
A first-timer like you has
no hope of getting out.

19:28.333 --> 19:31.086
Take one wrong turn
in the maze-like route,

19:31.170 --> 19:34.339
and you'll be running in circles
until you die here.

19:39.553 --> 19:42.347
That's a Kagemori agent
who tailed us in the past.

19:42.431 --> 19:47.728
He carelessly followed a Tadera,
got lost, and died here.

19:47.811 --> 19:49.980
There are more like him
all over the place.

19:50.564 --> 19:54.860
If you don't want to end up like them,
tell us who you are.

19:55.861 --> 19:56.820
Damn it.

19:56.904 --> 20:01.116
Hey, Dera. I still sense Daemons.

20:01.200 --> 20:02.784
Yeah, I bet.

20:02.868 --> 20:05.537
Those are the Tadera clan Daemons.

20:05.621 --> 20:07.331
What? The house?

20:07.915 --> 20:10.584
They create something
called the Lost House.

20:10.667 --> 20:12.711
Like Higashi Village, once you enter—

20:12.794 --> 20:13.670
No.

20:14.296 --> 20:16.256
Not those.

20:16.340 --> 20:17.841
There's another pair.

21:22.030 --> 21:23.448
Well, well.

21:23.532 --> 21:25.951
Well, well, well.

21:26.868 --> 21:29.454
If it isn't Right and Left.

21:30.747 --> 21:32.249
Yuru, Dera.

21:32.332 --> 21:34.126
Take these people and stand back.

21:43.719 --> 21:46.471
They're Tenaga-Ashinaga.

21:46.555 --> 21:48.932
